Changelog: 29-10-2026 00:18:23

Added. Your games, Memory cards and Log, the BC250 suite's PCSX2 Manager's other parts, as cards beside PCSX2 and
Settings (owner, 29-10-2026: "same as BC250, portable look"). Your games: the PS2 disc images (ISO, CHD, CSO, ZSO,
GZ) in the chosen folders and five below them, an ISO read for its serial and titled from PCSX2's own GameIndex.yaml
(resources\ in its folder); A plays a game alone and full screen (pcsx2-qt.exe -nogui -fullscreen -- <game>), X
marks it for Steam and Y Update Steam makes Steam's shortcuts match ("[PS2] <title>", PCSX2's own program with the
game, the pictures drawn from the app's icon or fetched from SteamGridDB with the suite's key in
%APPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\steamgriddb-key), Steam closed for it and started again; Folders offers the usual
places and the removable drives, and Windows' own folder window; a folder goes off the list with a second press. The
games, the catalog, the shortcuts and the memory card code (mymc++, as the BC250 app keeps it) are the BC250 app's,
with Windows' paths and process list. Memory cards: the cards in PCSX2's memcards folder with their slot, saves and
free space, a card's saves on A, New card (8 MB) and Copy card. Log: PCSX2's last run from its own log (the game,
the time played, the controllers), the play time in all, the newest lines of the app's log and Open the log. A long
list scrolls with the d-pad and a finger, the focused row kept in view. The window fits a screen smaller than the
handheld's, as every app of the suite.

