Changelog: 28-10-2026 21:24:56

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 28-10-2026 20:58:05

Added. PCSX2's settings (owner, 28-10-2026: next the settings, set up as the BC250 suite's PCSX2 Manager does, so its
lessons need not be learned again). The window has two cards, PCSX2 and Settings, with their panes beside them, as
Windows Portable Test. After an install, when the window opens and before PCSX2 opens, the app keeps what it owns in
PCSX2's inis\PCSX2.ini, starting from PCSX2 2.8.2's own defaults (pcsx2_defaults.ini, the file it wrote at its
first start on the Ally) when there is none: the setup wizard done, PCSX2's own updates off, the mouse pointer
hidden in a game, the BIOS in its bios folder, player 1 on the handheld's controller (SDL-0, by the buttons' places)
while no controller is mapped, View + Menu to quit a game, and Big Picture mode full screen (StartBigPictureMode and
StartFullscreen: tried on the Ally, PCSX2 opens its controller menu full screen). The quit chord and Big Picture
stay off once turned off; every other line stays as PCSX2 wrote it, with its CRLF line ends. The Settings pane has a
pill per setting with its value, A steps to the next one and writes it at once: Renderer (Automatic, Direct3D 12,
Direct3D 11, Vulkan, OpenGL, Software), Resolution (Native to 4x), VSync, Show FPS, Fast boot, Vibration, Player 2,
Quit with Select + Start and Big Picture; what each does is behind the information icon. Nothing is written while
this folder's PCSX2 runs (Windows' process list and the program's path: it writes its settings back when it closes);
Open PCSX2 says when it is open already.

Fixed. PCSX2's first start showed its setup wizard, with its own updates ticked, and left the controller unmapped:
the install wrote no settings (the BC250 suite's lesson of 23-10-2026). The settings are now written right after the
install, before PCSX2 first opens. The release carries pcsx2_defaults.ini (the suite's build adds a package's data
files).

Changelog: 28-10-2026 20:35:50

Added. PCSX2 installed and opened (owner, 28-10-2026: installing PCSX2 first). A on Install downloads PCSX2 2.8.2
for Windows (pcsx2-v2.8.2-windows-x64-Qt.7z, 26 MB) from PCSX2's release on GitHub, checks it against the pinned
SHA-256 and unpacks it with Windows' own tar.exe into
%LOCALAPPDATA%\windows-portable-suite\windows-portable-pcsx2\emulator\, in PCSX2's portable mode (portable.txt): its
settings, BIOS, memory cards and save states stay in that folder. The page counts the megabytes; B during the download asks first. A on Open PCSX2 starts it detached. Remove,
with a second press, deletes only the files the release brought (installed.json lists them). When PCSX2 replaced its
program with another build (its own updater), the page says so and Y Reinstall puts 2.8.2 back. install.ps1
--uninstall keeps PCSX2's folder, --purge removes it too.

